      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There is no single definitive answer, as the concept of the \"line\" is precisely where modern philosophical debate still flourishes. However, most contemporary scholars reject the idea that this expansion is a mere \"necessary evolution,\" arguing instead that unchecked surveillance fundamentally alters the terms of the original consent. Instead of being a settled point, the debate often centers on establishing rigorous, enforceable limits to ensure that security measures remain proportional and accountable to the populace.",
      "source": "target",
